From 8f806215906607a4d7e456ccba3680de327ef11b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:25:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): touch-only notify subs no longer keep a chat
 busy or red [daveey]

A comment/unblock/link on someone else's card auto-subscribes the chat
(kanban.auto_subscribe_on_touch). kanban_session_activity counted every tui
sub toward kanban_active/kanban_blocked, so one comment on a scheduled soak
kept the row busy for days and a needs_input card painted the toucher red.

Subs now carry delivery_metadata.reason: create (kanban_create auto-sub),
touch (auto-sub on touch) or shepherd (explicit tui notify-subscribe, which
also upgrades an earlier touch). A sub counts toward active/blocked, the
Tasks view and attention only when the chat owns the card or the reason is
create/shepherd. Legacy subs without a reason count only for the owner, so
existing touch subs stop counting at once. Subs are never deleted:
completion pings still fire.
